node3 (RHEL7), loaded it with application data, then added node4 as a fourth member which received the full dataset via SST and accepted writes that replicated back to the original members. Completed the mandatory node-restart protocol for all four nodes, one at a time with quorum preserved, verifying changed boot identity and full cluster/data recovery after each restart.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Configured MariaDB 10.11 archive yum repo and EPEL (for pv dependency) on node1-node4 (RHEL7)\",\"Installed MariaDB-server, MariaDB-client, galera-4, MariaDB-shared on all four nodes\",\"Opened firewalld ports 3306, 4567/tcp+udp, 4568, 4444 on all four nodes\",\"Wrote /etc/my.cnf.d/galera.cnf on node1-node3 with a 3-node gcomm cluster address and unique wsrep_node_name/address per node\",\"Bootstrapped Galera on node1 (galera_new_cluster), then started mariadb on node2 and node3 to join via rsync SST; confirmed wsrep_cluster_size=3, Synced\",\"Enabled mariadb service on node1-node3; generated a root password on node1 and applied via ALTER USER, which replicated cluster-wide via Galera TOI\",\"Created appdata.orders table with sample rows on node1; verified replication to node2 and node3\",\"Updated wsrep_cluster_address on node1-node3 to include node4; wrote galera.cnf on node4 with the 4-node gcomm address\",\"Enabled and started mariadb on node4; it joined via SST, received the full dataset, and reached wsrep_cluster_size=4, Synced, Primary\",\"Distributed root credentials to node2/node3/node4 over SSH using CLUSTER_SSH_PUBKEY/PRIVKEY, then removed the transient copies from the antrieb home directories\",\"Performed a write (INSERT) on node4 and confirmed it replicated back to node1, proving node4 accepts writes like the other members\",\"Captured a healthy baseline (boot_id, wsrep status, row counts) on all four nodes\",\"Restarted node1, polled until reachable, confirmed changed boot_id and full Galera/data resync before moving to the next node\",\"Repeated the same restart-verify sequence for node2, node3, and node4, preserving 3-of-4 quorum throughout\",\"Performed a final cross-cluster check confirming cluster_size=4, Primary status, and consistent replicated data on all nodes after all four restarts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Three-member Galera cluster running on node1, node2, node3 holding application data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-544ea682f4b444dc\",\"cmd-b5fc551be00f41f5\",\"cmd-eb2aee629bf845fd\",\"cmd-7f1d83fd4e894d31\",\"cmd-fb5c7d4ce41e4f9b\",\"cmd-03987f226c8f40cf\"],\"summary\":\"node1 bootstrapped (cluster_size=1, Primary); node2 and node3 joined via SST reaching cluster_size=2 then 3, Synced; appdata.orders created on node1 with sample rows and confirmed present on node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 added as a fourth member carrying existing data\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-838a401ff196401b\",\"cmd-5140d34aa2a84521\",\"cmd-15ba3b24e0964368\"],\"summary\":\"node4 configured with 4-node gcomm address, started, joined via SST, reached wsrep_cluster_size=4/Synced/Primary with the pre-existing appdata.orders rows visible\"},{\"requirement\":\"node4 accepts writes like the other members\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-5d7cbd20da4548ce\",\"cmd-85840a1515734193\"],\"summary\":\"INSERT executed directly on node4 succeeded and the new row was visible when queried from node1, proving bidirectional replication\"},{\"requirement\":\"Healthy baseline captured on every node before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-29a45497d81943eb\",\"cmd-3a8fbbfa029a4ca2\",\"cmd-95fc772c86364e43\",\"cmd-cda336b626b24ecf\"],\"summary\":\"Captured boot_id, uptime -s, wsrep_cluster_size/status, and appdata.orders row count on node1-node4 prior to any restarts\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovery\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c6b1a53200a24e13\",\"cmd-25c5f9e8db1f4c55\",\"cmd-c53769bfa4424e5e\",\"cmd-878702ce451e4f84\"],\"summary\":\"Reboot acknowledged before disconnect; node unreachable mid-re